# The two-way bus, written into memory by asteroid. Structure only: no counts, no Python.
# Design in workshop/bus/README.md. Readings are open; the one check below is the route forest it stands on.
check "python3 -I workshop/route/route.py"
frame "Two-way bus: OUT from programs down to memory, IN from memory back up (workshop/bus/README.md)" reading "a design reading: the two trees run opposite ways" -> none label open reach 1 cost 40
frame "Layer order: no bus edge skips a layer (programs, evidence, memory)" reading "a design rule to be checked; not yet a claim" -> none label open reach 1 cost 40
frame "Spiral sync: OUT, IN, OUT until no edge is pruned (a fixed point)" reading "a design rule; the fixed point is not yet checked by asteroid" -> none label open reach 1 cost 40
record workshop/bus bus checked-finite "The two-way bus (on the route forest checked above): OUT (programs to memory) and IN (memory to programs) share one pruned edge set, pruned by layer order and first parent; the spiral runs OUT, IN, OUT to a fixed point. Only the route forest is checked; the bus laws are design, not yet checked."
